##### MF2: RESONANCE PARAMETERS                                   7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT151    : Resonance parameters                                 7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
Resonance parameters were imported from JEFF3.1.1 up to 2 keV.    7328 1451
Parameters were taken from [mug73, mac84] for positive resonances 7328 1451
from ENDF/B-IV for a negative resonance. The radiative width of   7328 1451
0.059ev was assumed for the resonance whose radiative width       7328 1451
was unknown.                                                      7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
##### MF3: REACTION CROSS SECTIONS                                7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
All the data present in the following MT-sections have been       7328 1451
calculated with Talys. If the maximal cross section in an         7328 1451
excitation function over the whole energy range does not exceed   7328 1451
1.e-9 b, the MT-number is not included at all. Cross sections     7328 1451
lower than 1.e-20 b are assumed to have no physical meaning and   7328 1451
are set to zero. Not all of the following MT-numbers may be       7328 1451
present for this isotope, because this depends on Q-values.       7328 1451
They are all listed for completeness.                             7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT1      : Total cross section                                  7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
Below 2 keV: from the resonance fit.                              7328 1451
Above 2 keV: Calculated with the optical model.                   7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT2      : Elastic scattering cross section                     7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
Obtained by subtracting the non-elastic cross section from the    7328 1451
total cross section.                                              7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT3      : Non-elastic cross section                            7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
Calculated with the optical model over the whole energy range.    7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT4      : Total inelastic cross section                        7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
Sum of MT=51-91.                                                  7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT5      : (n,anything) cross section                           7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
For energies below 20 MeV, MT5 contains the lumped (n,gamma x)    7328 1451
cross section, where x may represent neutron, proton, deuteron,   7328 1451
triton, Helium-3 or alpha. Using the relative yields of MF6/MT5,  7328 1451
the (n,gamma n), (n,gamma p), ..., (n,gamma alpha) can be         7328 1451
recovered. These cross sections are relatively small. However,    7328 1451
addition of these cross sections, which can not be stored in any  7328 1451
other MT-number, ensures that the partial cross sections add up   7328 1451
to the non-elastic cross section. Above 20 MeV, MT5 contains the  7328 1451
total non-elastic cross section, with which the information of    7328 1451
MF6/MT5 can be combined to obtain particle production cross       7328 1451
sections and (double-)differential cross sections.                7328 1451
                                                                  7328 1451
- MT11     : (n,2nd) cross section                                7328 1451
- MT16     : (n,2n) cross section                                 7328 1451
- MT17     : (n,3n) cross section                                 7328 1451
- MT22     : (n,na) cross section                                 7328 1451
